column14:
In every Objective-C API I've seen that uses blocks, the framework takes care of the "[[... copy] autorelease]" bit.  In practice, the code looks something like (to borrow your block with foos and bars):<p><pre><code>    [array transformFoos:^(Foo*) (Foo* bar) {
        return bar;
    }];
</code></pre>
I'm not sure there is a more succinct way to write a lambda with typed arguments and a typed return value.
